
# ── AI (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The written report brief and the chat assistant. Everything else — the verdict
# engine, the maps, the area data — works with none of these set.
#
# The chain tries providers in this order and uses the first that is configured
# AND answers; a failing one is stepped past automatically. Free tiers first.
#
# NOTE ON DATA: free tiers generally reserve the right to train on what you send,
# and these requests carry a user's property figures and building location. The
# PDPO statement on /privacy names classes of transferees — update it before
# pointing this at real users' data. See packages/api/src/ai.ts.
#
# ── A LOCAL MODEL (Ollama / LM Studio) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint. Tried first, so it beats every provider below.
# No API key needed: for this entry the URL is what makes it configured, and the
# Authorization header is omitted entirely when AI_API_KEY is blank.
#
#   ollama serve
#   ollama pull llama3.1:8b
#   AI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1
#   AI_MODEL=llama3.1:8b
#
# This is the only option that sends nothing anywhere: the property figures never
# leave the machine, which answers the data concern above outright.
#
# ⚠ WORKS IN LOCAL DEV ONLY. Vercel functions run on Vercel's servers and cannot
#   reach 127.0.0.1 on your laptop — set this in production and the chain records
#   "fetch failed" and falls through to the next provider. To use a local model in
#   production you must either expose it on a public HTTPS URL (a tunnel, or a VPS
#   you host it on) or run the app somewhere that can see it.
AI_BASE_URL=
AI_API_KEY=
AI_MODEL=
# Free tiers
GROQ_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
CEREBRAS_API_KEY=
MISTRAL_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Paid fallback
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Model ids drift; override any of these if a provider 404s the default.
# GROQ_MODEL=   GEMINI_MODEL=   CEREBRAS_MODEL=   MISTRAL_MODEL=
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=   ANTHROPIC_MODEL=
